RK3528 (HINLINK OPC-H28K) thermal sensor support.

The 5.4 rockchip_thermal driver knows nothing about rockchip,rk3528-tsadc, so the
SoC's tsadc node never probes and no thermal zone appears (LuCI then shows NaN).
Instead of hand-stitching ~50 register macros and 8 helper functions out of the
vendor BSP 5.10 driver, take that file whole: it is a superset (all eight
compatibles we already support, plus rk3528/rk3562/rk3568/rk3588/...) and it
brings the OTP trim calibration (nvmem-cells trim_l/trim_h) that makes the
reading accurate.

Two small adaptations for 5.4:
  * a compat shim for thermal_zone_device_enable()/_disable() (5.5 API; a zone
    is live right after registration on 5.4, so both are no-ops), and
  * the vendor file's <linux/rockchip/cpu.h> (used only for the px30s/rk3308bs
    variant checks) is provided by files/include/linux/rockchip/cpu.h, so the
    driver source itself stays otherwise untouched.

Note on the vendor's #ifdef CONFIG_CPU_* guards around every of_device_id
entry: those are BSP-private Kconfig symbols that do not exist in this tree, so
with them in place the match table compiles to nothing and no board matches at
all.  They are removed here, i.e. all SoC data is always compiled and matching
is done purely from the DT - the same behaviour as the mainline driver.

